# the argument of aristotle-ethics-4.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
logic	kd
# "should" and "must" are read throughout as obligation (ought).
# S1 (honour to elders, frankness to companions) lists duties the conclusion is not drawn from, so it is left out.
atom	render_due	we render to those of the same family, tribe or city, and all similarly connected with us, their due
atom	discriminate	we discriminate what belongs to each in respect of nearness of connection, goodness or intimacy
atom	same_class_easier	in the case of those of the same class the discrimination is easier
atom	diff_class_harder	in the case of those who are in different classes the discrimination is a matter of more trouble
atom	give_up	we give up the attempt to discriminate
atom	observe_practicable	we observe the distinctions so far as it is practicable to do so
P1	S2	O render_due ∧ O discriminate	kind normative
P2	S2	same_class_easier ∧ diff_class_harder	kind empirical
# S3: the greater trouble "should not be a reason for giving up the attempt"; read as: though it is harder, since we ought to discriminate, we ought not give up.
P3	S3	diff_class_harder ∧ O discriminate → O ¬give_up	kind normative
A1	-	O discriminate → O observe_practicable	kind normative
C	S3	O ¬give_up ∧ O observe_practicable	from P1 P2 P3 A1
